# The shelf holds what the agents produce, and most of it is versioned. Handoffs
# are the exception: CSTs are transient by design (deleted on ingest; nothing
# auto-deletes — `handoff-store list` age-flags strays), they are chmod 600, and
# they carry raw conversation context. Tracking a
# file built to delete itself is churn; tracking one built to hold session
# contents is worse.
home/.claude/shelf/handoffs/
home/.claude/shelf/boot-digest.stamp
# sline rewrites it on every render
home/.claude/shelf/cc-usage-window.json

# yt-transcripts are the shelf's second exception, for the same reason as handoffs:
# they are bulky downloads (a 50-min talk is ~550 KB of raw .vtt), they re-download
# from youtube in seconds, and the skill's `transit` mode deletes them on purpose.
# Tracking a store one of whose modes is "delete immediately" is pure churn.
home/.claude/shelf/yt-transcripts/

# The sounds shelf holds game audio Dima ripped by hand — assets we have no
# right to redistribute, and binaries git has no business storing. audition.sh
# is the only thing here we wrote; approved.txt and candidates/ are his picking
# state, rebuilt by running the TUI again.
home/.claude/shelf/sounds/*
!home/.claude/shelf/sounds/audition.sh

# The cclio-mode snapshot is a build (script/skill-cclio-mode-snapshot.ts), recompiled at every halt.
home/.claude/shelf/cclio-mode-snapshot.md

# The memory-sync mirror is a build too (script/skill-memory-sync-mirror.ts): the cc masters rendered
# into cw memory entries plus a manifest, re-rendered by pnpm memory-sync:copy / skill:memory-sync-mirror.
home/.claude/shelf/memory-sync-mirror/
__pycache__/
home/.claude/shelf/ci-seen.json
home/.claude/shelf/pr-watch-seen.json
home/.claude/shelf/jev/route.log
home/.claude/shelf/jev/runs.log
home/.claude/shelf/jev/router.off
home/.claude/shelf/jev/replays/
home/.claude/shelf/jev/spend.log
home/.claude/shelf/barrel-probe.log

# Runtime state written by scheduled jobs, not source. The cowork gazette heartbeat
# is written on anthropic's machines and lands here; nothing in the repo produces it.
schedule/state/

# The scan snapshot the daemon hands the chords app, rewritten by `pnpm hotkeys:scan`. A
# picture of this mac's app preferences, not source — and biome reformats it while the
# generator re-emits raw json, so committing it means a tree that is dirty after every scan.
# The page says which command is missing when it is absent.
hotkeys/hotkeys.json
hotkeys/chords/dist/
speak/dist/
# impeccable live resolves the app root from the repo root and leaves its manifest here. The
# rest of its state is ignored by the .gitignore live writes and maintains inside the app.
.impeccable/live/

# gmailctl's oauth client and token live beside the config it reads; secrets, never source.
gmail/credentials.json
gmail/token.json

# impeccable-ignore-start
# Ephemeral output, runtime state, and per-dev overrides.
# `**/` on every line: a pattern holding a `/` is anchored to the repo root, so the readme's
# bare form misses a nested workspace (apps/proto-lab/.impeccable/…) — measured 2026-09-19.
# Shared artifacts stay tracked: config.json, live/config.json,
# design.json, surfaces/*.md, critique/*.md.
**/.impeccable/config.local.json
**/.impeccable/hook.cache.json
**/.impeccable/hook.pending.json
**/.impeccable/*.png
**/.impeccable/review/
**/.impeccable/questions/
**/.impeccable/live/server.json
**/.impeccable/live/sessions/
**/.impeccable/live/previews/
**/.impeccable/live/annotations/
**/.impeccable/live/cache/
**/.impeccable/live/manual-edit-apply-transaction.json
**/.impeccable/live/manual-edit-events.jsonl
**/.impeccable/live/manual-edit-evidence/
**/.impeccable/live/pending-manual-edits.json
**/.impeccable/live/deferred-svelte-component-accepts.json
**/.impeccable/live/*.png
# impeccable-ignore-end

